The float32 kernels, sparse contact accumulation, chunk scheduling and event
recording adapt portions of Kiyan Doguc's MIT-licensed implementation:
https://github.com/Kisame76/drosophila-brain-mlx
Revision: e417b33616513ef350b1b1c3cdf2b5b7a1799c8e.
The full original notice is in Kisame76-LICENSE.

Local adaptations use Eon's v783 graph contract and SI units, preserve ordered
duplicate stimulation channels, and expose bounded recording and independent
qualification observations. Eon's repository licensing declarations remain
unchanged, subject to applicable third-party notices.

The scientific model and parameters originate with Shiu et al.'s leaky
integrate-and-fire Drosophila model. The donor credits Brian2's generated
linear-update coefficients and mehrantsi/flyBrain's sparse/fused-kernel ideas.
This directory contributes an execution implementation, not new model or data.
